# Port patch, second player test (26.11.2026, the project owner: split screen and online need a second Leon; this is the
# first experiment of port/docs/split-online-plan.md). While the app sends a controller on channel 1 (re4_pad2_connected,
# runtime/pad.cpp) the main loop creates a second Leon (EmMgr.create(0), the constructor sets pPL = this, so pPL is put
# back) beside the first one and moves it after the first player (re4_pl2_move, em.cpp): the game reads the globals pPL
# and Key, so pPL and Key are swapped to the second player's (Key2, built from Joy[1] in pad.cpp) for that one call and
# put back. emMove skips the second player (the first one is skipped there too); cEmMgr::destroy / arrayAlloc forget it.
# Without a controller on channel 1 nothing changes: no second player, no Key2 effect. NOT done yet: the camera (follows
# the first player only), the enemies' targets (pTarget = pPL), the HUD, the inventory and life (shared: pG), cutscenes.
